  "report_period": "Week 36 (28th Aug to 4th Sep 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Navios Maritime Partners have committed their Capesize \"Navios Pollux\" 180/2009 Stx, Korea (SS 07/2029, DD 11/2026, Scrubber fitted) at USD 30,75 mill. Note that back in July, the one-year-younger \"Nicholas G.S\" 179/2010 Sungdong, Korea (SS 07/2030, DD 02/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed at USD 34,5 mill. Furthermore, the \"Erato\" 180/2010 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 09/2027, Scrubber fitted) of Lavinia Corp was committed at USD 38 mill, while the one-year-younger \"Mount Dampier\" 181/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 11/2026, Scrubber fitted) was committed a week ago at xs USD 38 mill. Japanese owners committed the Post Panamax \"Kiyo\" 92/2012 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 01/2031, DD 02/2029) to undisclosed interests at low USD 19 mill. For reference, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Ohshu Maru\" 92/2011 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) was sold back in April at USD 16,2 mill. The Kamsarmax \"KM Mt. Jade\" 81/2008 Universal, Japan (SS 10/2028, DD 11/2026) of Kuang Ming Shipping was committed to Chinese interests at xs USD 16 mill. Remind you that a couple of months ago, the one-year-younger \"C. S. Olive\" 82/2009 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 06/2029, DD 05/2027) was sold at USD 17 mill. On the Supramax sector, Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha committed their \"Stenia Colossus\" 58/2011 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 03/2031, DD 04/2029) at USD 21 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Sunny Royal\" 58/2011 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 11/2030, DD 12/2028) was sold back in April at USD 18,5 mill. Moreover, Precious Shipping committed their \"Kanchana Naree\" 56/2011 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 10/2026) to Chinese interests at USD 14,6 mill, while the two- years-older sister vessel \"FLC Happiness\" 56/2009 Taizhou, China (SS 08/2029, DD 09/2027) was also committed to Chinese interests at USD 12,9 mill. Korean owners have committed the Handysize \"T Prime\" 32/2011 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 12/2026) to undisclosed interests at USD 9,5 mill. By way of comparison, the \"Seamec Gallant\" 32/2011 Jiangmen, China (SS/DD 10/2026) was sold in July at the same price.",
    "tankers": "Following the sale of the MR2 \"Minerva Rita\" 50/2005 Stx, Korea (SS 10/2030, DD 09/2028, Ice Class 1A) back in July at USD 16,2 mill, clients of Minerva Marine have now committed the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Minerva Xanthe\" 50/2006 Stx, Korea (SS 07/2031, DD 10/2028, Ice Class 1A) to Chinese interests at USD 16 mill. In addition, Cido Shipping committed the \"Gran Couva\" 47/2008 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2028, DD 11/2026) at USD 19,25 mill, while the one-year-older \"Rui Fu Sheng\" 46/2007 Sungdong, Korea (SS 01/2031, DD 01/2029) was committed at xs USD 19 mill. Note that in August, the \"Atlantic Eagle\" 47/2007 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 12/2027) was sold at xs USD 18 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route strengthened significantly, with Port Hedland and Dampier to Qingdao fixtures settling between USD 15.25/18.00 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul departures from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, achieved between USD 38.50/41.00 fio, alongside a Seven Islands run reaching USD 46.80 fio. Transatlantic activity saw runs from PDM and Port Cartier to Ijmuiden and Fos fixing between USD 20.00/21.00 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with India and Singapore-Japan options settled between USD 16,750/23,750 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan and South East Asia ranges fetched between USD 18,000/24,500 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China and Singapore-Japan achieved between USD 14,000/24,000 pd. From Persian Gulf, West Coast India and East Coast India, trips via South Africa to India obtained between USD 22,500/27,000 pd, while trips via ECSA to Far East destinations fixed between USD 19,000/24,500 pd. In the Atlantic, a NCSA departure via USEC to Continent range reached USD 23,000 pd. On period, short to medium-term fixtures for 5 to 12 months duration settled between USD 18,750/23,000 pd, while a longer 24 months period was secured at USD 19,500 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, an Indonesian coal run to Thailand achieved USD 22,000 pd, while a clinker trip from South China to Chittagong reached USD 28,000 pd and a cement trip to East Africa fetched USD 23,000 pd. Out of West Coast India, regional runs to West Coast India and Bangladesh fixed between USD 14,500/20,000 pd, alongside coastal India trips from East Coast India obtaining USD 21,000 pd, while a long-haul trip to China settled at USD 11,000 pd. Out of West Africa, long-haul ore and agricultural runs to China were agreed between USD 23,500/27,000 pd. From South Africa, departures to India and China secured between USD 18,000/24,000 pd, alongside ballast bonuses from USD 180,000 to USD 270,000. In the Atlantic, ECSA front-haul trips to South East Asia and Singapore-Japan range obtained between USD 19,000/19,500 pd, with ballast bonuses between USD 900,000 and USD 950,000. Transatlantic grain and woodpellet runs from USEC and US Gulf reached USD 30,000 pd and USD 27,500 pd respectively, while Continent departures to the Mediterranean range settled between USD 22,000/22,500 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Pacific, East Australia runs to South East Asia fetched between USD 19,500/20,000 pd, a USWC trip via NoPac to Singapore-Japan obtained USD 17,000 pd and a WCI departure to ECI settled at USD 15,000 pd. Out of South Africa, front-haul runs to Far East destinations achieved between USD 13,850/15,000 pd, a trip to WCI made USD 13,500 pd and a transatlantic run to Continent secured USD 16,000 pd. In the Atlantic, departures from USEC and USG to Continent and EC Mexico options fixed at USD 14,000 pd and USD 13,750 pd respectively."
    }
  },
